"Let $G$ be a bipartite graph, let $d_u$ denote the degree of $u\\in V(G)$, and let $H$ be a loop-graph. Write $\\hom(G,H)$ for the number of graph homomorphisms from $G$ to $H$. **Galvin's biregular homomorphism conjecture.**\n\n$$\n\\hom(G,H)\\le \\prod_{uv\\in E(G)}\\hom(K_{d_u,d_v},H)^{1/(d_ud_v)}.\n$$\n\nThis would extend the regular and biregular homomorphism inequalities, as well as the bipartite case of Kahn's irregular independent-set conjecture. Its status is open."